<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amir Husayn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1370</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amir Husayn was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaraunas">Qara'unas</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazaghan">Qazaghan</a>, who dominated the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> in the 1360s. He allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> against the Moghuls of the eastern khanate, but the two became rivals. In 1370 Timur besieged him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a>, where he was killed, and Timur took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amir-husayn.jpg" alt="Amir Husayn" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timur_during_attack_on_Balkh_1370.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
